{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And they were in his eyes like a few days.</b> It would have been fitting that they be in his eyes like many days, but with regard to the burden of the labor he said thus, for they were in his reckoning 'a few days' — not a count of years and not a count of months. And so he said, ״כי מלאו ימי״ (Genesis 29:21), and did not say 'my years'; and this is to diminish in his eyes the burden of the seven years."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:16:14.294853527Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}